  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nA second wire EDM post, `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps`, offered as \"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\" for machines declared `wire_edm`. It is never the default; the generic ISO wire post stays first.\r\n\r\n**The output was not run on a real Sodick control. It must be checked by someone with the machine before cutting.** Every posted program says so in its header (`NOT VERIFIED ON A CONTROL - CHECK BEFORE CUTTING`).\r\n\r\nThis is one slice: a vertical 2-axis Wire Contour. The program is:\r\n\r\n- header comments (machine name, not verified, wire-centre path, no `G92` written, tank and flushing not programmed)\r\n- `G21` or `G20`, `G90`\r\n- a header line: each C condition named below must exist in the control's condition table before start\r\n- per operation: a line naming its condition (`CONDITION C110 MUST EXIST IN THE CONTROL CONDITION TABLE - CHECK ITS VALUES`), the setup's `G54`-`G59`, `G40 G00 X Y` to the start hole (the wire offset is cancelled before any motion), `T91` (thread), the condition id as a `C` word, then `G01` / `G02` / `G03 X Y I J`, `T90` (cut the wire)\r\n- `M02`\r\n\r\nOn a machine with `edm.awt: false` the operator threads and cuts the wire at a stated `M00`. Every coordinate carries a decimal point.\r\n\r\nRefused by name, never posted: taper, 4-axis, a leaning or posed move, a rotary, a Z change, a rapid while threaded, a tool change, an rpm, a canned cycle, a non-XY arc, an arc without a centre, an arc as the first cut, a trip home, a non-wire machine or operation, a work offset outside `G54`-`G59`, a condition id that is not `C` and three digits, and a program that ends threaded.\r\n\r\nFiles: the script; `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (registry entry, `WIRE_POSTS`); `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs` and `wire_post.rs` (the tables learn the second wire post); `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`; new tests and goldens; `docs/decisions/617-sodick-wire-post.md`. No new dependency.\r\n\r\n## Sources\r\n\r\n- Sodick Inc., \"Wire EDM Machine Operation\" (copyright November 1998; A320D, A530, A530D, AP350, AP500, A600, A750, A1000; Mark 21 / EX21 control), read at manualslib.com/manual/2816797/Sodick-A320d.html: G, M and T code tables, the word list, the AWT sequence and the program examples.\r\n- RS-274 / ISO 6983 for the motion words.\r\n- This project's `wire-iso.cps` for the script's structure.\r\n\r\nNo other CAM product's post, post library or output was read. The sample program attached to the issue is another CAM's output and was not used.\r\n\r\n## Unconfirmed\r\n\r\nCheck each at the machine:\r\n\r\n- Whether the LN1W / LN2W controls of the AQ / AD / ALN series (the issue's machine is an AQ600L) read these Mark 21 words unchanged. No free official reference for the LN controls was found.\r\n- `G40` beside `G00` on the move to the threading point, with no offset active, in a program that never states `G41` / `G42`.\r\n- A program with no `G92` / `G29`, relying on the work offset set at the control.\r\n- Cutting with no flushing or tank word in the program.\r\n- No `%`, no program number, no `M30`.\r\n- The condition as a bare `C` word with no condition table rows in the file (the header and each section tell the operator to check it exists).\r\n- `M02` after `T90` leaving the machine safe.\r\n- The manual was read through a third-party-hosted copy by a summarising fetch, not page by page.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/sodick_wire_post.rs` (8 tests): `the_punch_contour_posts_its_sodick_golden_through_the_gate`, `the_registry_offers_the_sodick_post_for_wire_edms_only_and_never_by_default`, `taper_and_four_axis_are_refused_by_name`, `a_condition_id_that_is_not_a_sodick_c_word_is_refused_by_name`, `a_mill_machine_and_a_milling_section_are_refused_by_name`, `without_awt_the_operator_threads_and_cuts_at_a_stated_stop`, `an_inch_document_posts_g20_with_pointed_four_place_words`, `an_arc_posts_g03_with_incremental_i_j_and_never_as_the_first_cut`. New golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch.nc`.\r\n- `crates/post/tests/script_sodick_wire.rs`: the post on the 11 recorded edge-case streams, each a named refusal (new goldens in `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/sodick-wire/`).\r\n- Green on the head: every `camcraft-post` suite; `camcraft-app` lib plus the 38 suites that touch the post registry or wire work (`conformance`, `wire_post`, `posting`, `post_serves_kind`, `explain_option`, `smoothing`, `program_units`, `recorded_post_streams`, the `wire_*`, `plasma_*`, `coolant*` and lathe post suites among them); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\r\n- No existing golden or snapshot was changed.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- No Sodick control or simulator ran the output.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` as one command: its plan for this diff is every app suite (about 350 binaries). The suites above were run instead; the rest of app and all of `camcraft-ui` were not.\r\n- Taper and 4-axis only as refusals.\r\n- No UI test: the post appears through the existing post list. No real Sodick machine file exists yet (#1501); the tests use the wire EDM fixture machine.\r\n\r\n## Follow-ups\r\n\r\n- #1496 taper\r\n- #1497 4-axis\r\n- #1498 control-side wire offset and skim passes\r\n- #1499 tank and flushing words as parameters\r\n- #1500 confirm the LN-control program format\r\n- #1501 a Sodick machine file with sourced travels\r\n\r\nNo new command, so no MCP tool is owed.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Sodick wire EDM post (\"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\"): 2-axis wire contours in the words of Sodick's 1998 operation manual; taper and 4-axis are refused by name; not verified on a control.\r\n\r\n## Review fixes (second commit, 4276e97e8)\r\n\r\n- `G40` placement: moved from the first cut to the `G00` to the threading point, so a wire offset left by an earlier program cannot shift the positioning or threading. Source: the manual shows `G40` riding a move (`G40 Y-.02`); RS-274 / ISO 6983 put `G40` in its own modal group, so it may share a block with `G00`, and cancelling with no offset active is legal. No header line was needed for this.\r\n- Condition table: a header line says each C condition named below must exist in the control's condition table; each section names its own condition before its first motion. (A list of all conditions at the very top was dropped: the post writes as it reads, and splicing lines in afterwards would shift the section line ranges the engine records.)\r\n- Closing keyword: this PR now only refers to the issue (the post is unverified; the issue's machine is an LN-control AQ600L, #1500 open). **The first commit's message (8460431c7) still carries a closing keyword for the issue** (history is not rewritten): the merger must check that issue 617 stays open after the merge, and reopen it if GitHub closes it.\r\n\r\nEffort: max (no escalation)\r\n\r\nRefs #617\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
